              %path{:d => "M -19.889179 -29.481103 L 19.084932 -29.481103 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.988838,0,0,-0.988838,39.112478,36.69173)"}
              %path{:d => "M -2.487415 2.868338 C -2.033125 1.145988 -1.021836 0.336167 0.00130317 0.000387379 C -1.021836 -0.335392 -2.033125 -1.149163 -2.487415 -2.867564 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.988838,0,0,-0.988838,58.221368,65.844133)"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "36.505903", "xlink:href" => "#CGmqiHF_xpXA0-Dlbj3Ce8o-PK0=-glyph1-2", :y => "61.529351"}
              %path{:d => "M -19.889179 -20.004223 L 21.387984 19.396525 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-dasharray:3.34735,1.91277;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.988838,0,0,-0.988838,39.112478,36.69173)"}
              %path{:d => "M -2.488612 2.868653 C -2.032271 1.149656 -1.018573 0.334982 0.000703248 0.00104258 C -1.019732 -0.335656 -2.031846 -1.149971 -2.486445 -2.867814 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.715256,-0.682723,-0.682723,-0.715256,60.433803,17.348882)"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "26.304066", "xlink:href" => "#CGmqiHF_xpXA0-Dlbj3Ce8o-PK0=-glyph2-1", :y => "32.515869"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "33.867684", "xlink:href" => "#CGmqiHF_xpXA0-Dlbj3Ce8o-PK0=-glyph3-1", :y => "30.435355"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "32.351796", "xlink:href" => "#CGmqiHF_xpXA0-Dlbj3Ce8o-PK0=-glyph1-2", :y => "32.515869"}
          %p Yet another way to say this is that:
          #ByCovHomPreservingEpis.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is projective precisely if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(P,-)
              preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This generalizes the notion of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
              over a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              There are variations of the definition where “epimorphism” is replaced by some other type of morphism, such as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+epimorphism"} strong epimorphism
              or the left class in some
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal factorization system
              %strong regular projectives
              and so on. In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
              “projective” almost always means “regular projective.”
            %p
              If the ambient category has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              are those for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∃
                        %mo !
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \stackrel{\exists!}{\to} P
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+morphism"} projective morphism
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
              notion is that of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              There is also a stronger notion of projective object, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(C, -)
              preserves coequalizers. See more at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+objects"} connected objects
              with “projective” used in this stronger sense.
          #EnoughProjectives.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              %strong enough projectives
              if for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to X
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is projective.
            %p
              Equivalently: if every object admits a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+presentation"} projective presentation
          %p
            This terminology refers to the existence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolutions"} projective resolutions
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EnoughIsEnough"}
            below.
          %h3#InAbelianCats In abelian categories
          %p
            Projective objects and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            are of central interest in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolutions"} cofibrant resolutions
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+resolutions"} fibrant resolutions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+chain+complexes"} model structures on chain complexes
          %h4#EquivalentCharacterizationInAbelianCats Equivalent characterizations
          #EquivalenceOfDefinitionsInAbelian.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p The following are equivalent
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{A}
                  is a projective object (in that it has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
                  against
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ByCovHomPreservingEpis"}
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒜
                        %mo →
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X,-) : \mathcal{A} \to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              For every object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X,-)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is projective.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              %strong
                of prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfDefinitionsInAbelian"}
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi i
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to A \stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow} B \stackrel{p}{\to} C \to 0
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              together is equivalent to the statement that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = \ker(p)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X, -)
              is left exact, it preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
              and so
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X, i) = \ker(Hom(X, p))
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to  Hom(X,A)
                    \\stackrel{Hom(X,i)}{\to}
                    Hom(X,B)
                    \\stackrel{Hom(X,p)}{\to}
                    Hom(X,C)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore we are reduced to showing that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X,p)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is projective. But this is def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ByCovHomPreservingEpis"}
          %h4#projective_resolutions Projective resolutions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in \mathcal{A}
              an object, a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolution"} projective resolution
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Q N)_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Q N \to N
            %p
              (with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              regarded as a complex concentrated in degree 0) such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  this morphism is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
                  (this is what makes it a
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Q
                        %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Q
                        %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots \to (Q N)_1 \to (Q N)_0 \to N
                %p
                  being an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
              %li
                %p
                  all whose entries
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Q
                        %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Q N)_n
                  are projective objects.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              This means precisely that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q N \to N
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
              with respect to the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
              (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "model%20structure%20on%20chain%20complexes#StandardQuillenOnBounded"} here
          #EnoughIsEnough.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              has
              %em enough projectives
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EnoughProjectives"}
          %h2#examples Examples
          #ProjectiveInSetsIsAxiomOfChoice.num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              can be phrased as “all objects of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              are projective.”
            %p
              See also
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internally+projective+object"} internally projective object
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullbacks
              and epimorphisms are preserved by pullback, as is the case in a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is projective iff any epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q\to P
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+epimorphism"} split
          #ProjectiveObjectsInAbAreFreeGroups.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              An object in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free group
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct summand
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
              for more on this.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              The projective objects in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} Hausdorff topological spaces
              are precisely the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremally+disconnected+profinite+sets"} extremally disconnected profinite sets
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              The projective objects in the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
              and order-preserving functions are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete"} discrete
              posets.
            %p
              Indeed, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be a poset and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(P)
              be the discrete poset with the same underlying set. Then the identity function on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is order-preserving from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(P)
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is projective, then this function admits an order-preserving section, which must also be the identity function. It follows that two elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              are comparable if and only if they are comparable in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(P)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is discrete.
            %p
              If we require projective objects to only satisfy the lifting property with respect to
              %em regular
              epimorphisms, then the projective objects can be characterised by forbidden subobjects: a poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is projective if and only if it does not admit any order-preserving injections from the 3-element chain, or from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+span"} walking span
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1 \geq 0 \leq 1'\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/undirected+graph"} undirected graph
              has no paths with three distinct vertices, if and only if it is the disjoint union of copies of the singleton poset and the two-element chain. Furthermore, every poset is a quotient of such a projective poset.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              By an argument similar to the previous example’s, every projective object in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} category of small categories
              is a discrete category.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              In the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
              and linear contractions, the only projective object is the zero space. If we require only lifting along regular epimorphisms, then all the
              = succeed "-spaces" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell^1
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ExistenceOfEnoughProjectives Existence of enough projectives
          %p
            We list examples of classes of categories that have enough projectives according to def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EnoughProjectives"}
          #ModHasEnoughProjectives.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Assuming the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              has enough projectives.
          %p
            See
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
            for more.
          #FreeModulesAreProjective.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Assuming the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \simeq R^{(S)}
              is projective.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveInSetsIsAxiomOfChoice"}
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
            %p
              More explicitly: if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(S) = R^{(S)}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(S) \to N
              is specified equivalently by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : S \to U(N)
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to the underlying set of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^{(S)} \simeq \oplus_{s \in S} R
              of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert S\vert}
              copies of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              Accordingly then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde N \to N
              an epimorphism, the underlying function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\tilde N) \to U(N)
              is an epimorphism, and by remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveInSetsIsAxiomOfChoice"}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              says that we have all lifts
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mi N
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; U(\tilde N)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\tilde f} \nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    S &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; U(N)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              these are equivalently lifts of module homomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi N
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi R
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi S
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \tilde N
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    R^{(S)} &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; N
                    }
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              %strong
                of prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModHasEnoughProjectives"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in R Mod
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(N) \in Set
              its underlying set, consider the
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi R
                      %mo )
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\oplus_{n \in U(N)} R
                    \\right)
                    \\to
                    N
            %p
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert U(N)\vert}
              copies of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in R_{n}
              of the
              = succeed "-labeled" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              to the corresponding element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              (and is thus fixed on all other elements by
              = succeed "-linearity)." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              This is clearly a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
              and by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeModulesAreProjective"}
              it is a surjection out of a projective object.
          %p
            A slightly subtle point is that there is no guarantee that the free module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F U(M)
            is actually projective, unless one assumes some form of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(E)
            of abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            in a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            (even though one can construct
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+resolutions"} free resolutions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
          %p
            There are however weak forms of the axiom of choice that hold in many toposes, such as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentation+axiom"} presentation axiom
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
          #EnoughWithCOSHEP.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-pretopos"} W-pretopos
              that satisfies
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/COSHEP"} COSHEP
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(E)
              has enough projectives.
          %p
            The idea of the proof is that under COSHEP, the underlying object of an abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            admits an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            from a projective object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon X \to U(A)
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) \to A
            is an epimorphism out of a projective in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(E)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi F
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ε
                        %mi A
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(X) \stackrel{F(p)}{\to} F U(A) \stackrel{\varepsilon_A}{\to} A
          %p
            (the first is epic because left adjoints preserve epis, whereas the second map, the component of the counit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ε
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi F
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon \colon F U \to id
            at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is faithful).
